        rubric: Choose float32 clamp and describe clamping. A comparison is optional.
        reply: {"answer":"The operation that clips your float32 sensor readings to the interval [-1, 1] is the **clamp** operation. It enforces the bounds exactly as you specified, preserving NaN payloads and handling edge cases like infinities and signed zeros according to IEEE rules. The clamp operation uses the numeric rules defined in the catalog, which include ordered clipping with bit-preserving ties and NaNs, and supports SIMD variants like SIMDPartial and SIMDMinMax. If you need to apply this operation, you can use the clamp group with the appropriate method (e.g., SIMDPartial or SIMDMinMax) depending on your SIMD strategy."}
